                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose incorporating a                           
                    skin‐tone balanced sampler in the                           
                    training DataLoader by computing                            
                    per‐sample weights inversely                                
                    proportional to the frequency of each                       
                    skin‐tone group and using a                                 
                    `WeightedRandomSampler`. This will                          
                    ensure each batch has equal                                 
                    representation of all skin tones,                           
                    improving fairness and potentially                          
                    boosting overall generalization. We'll                      
                    apply this change in both the                               
                    cross‐validation folds and the final                        
                    full‐data retraining.                                       
                    Results: The training script                                
                    successfully trained a DenseNet121                          
                    model for skin lesion malignancy                            
                    classification with a mean                                  
                    cross-validation AUROC of approximately                     
                    0.8975, indicating strong overall                           
                    performance. The code incorporates a                        
                    fairness approach by using a weighted                       
                    sampler to balance skin tone                                
                    representation during training. The                         
                    model was then retrained on the full                        
                    dataset and saved for inference. The                        
                    prediction function loads the saved                         
                    model and outputs malignancy                                
                    probabilities for new images as                             
                    required.                                                   
