                    Design: I propose adding a                                  
                    WeightedRandomSampler to balance                            
                    skin‐tone groups during training by                         
                    assigning each sample an                                    
                    inverse‐frequency weight based on its                       
                    skin tone. This will force each batch                       
                    to have equal representation of light                       
                    and dark skin tones, reducing fairness                      
                    gaps without altering overall dataset                       
                    size. We compute these weights per fold                     
                    (and for the full retrain) and replace                      
                    `shuffle=True` with the sampler in the                      
                    DataLoader. The rest of the pipeline                        
                    remains the same, and we report the                         
                    mean CV AUROC to evaluate impact.                           
