                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I will balance skin‐tone                            
                    representation by using a                                   
                    `WeightedRandomSampler` in the training                     
                    DataLoader, assigning each sample an                        
                    inverse‐frequency weight based on its                       
                    `skin_tone` label. This ensures each                        
                    batch sees equal numbers of light and                       
                    dark skin images, improving fairness                        
                    without altering total training data. I                     
                    apply this in both the 5‐fold CV loops                      
                    and the final full‐data retraining,                         
                    keeping the rest of the pipeline                            
                    (model, augmentations, TTA) unchanged.                      
                    Code: import os                                             
                    import torch                                                
                    import torch.nn as nn                                       
                    import torch.optim as optim                                 
                    from torch.utils.data import Dataset,                       
                    DataLoader, WeightedRandomSampler                           
